    <statement><p>Find <m>dy/dx</m> in terms of <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> 
if
<m>\arctan(x^{4} y) = x y^{4}</m>.</p>
<p><m>{dy\over dx} =</m> <fillin characters="65" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{4x^{4-1}y-y^{4}-x^{2\cdot 4}y^{4+2}}{4xy^{4-1}+4x^{2\cdot 4+1}y^{4+1}-x^{4}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x</m>.
<me>\frac{1}{(1 + x^{8} y^2)} (4 x^{3} y + x^{4} \frac{dy}{dx}) =
    y^{4} + 4 x y^{3} \frac{dy}{dx},</me>
so, clearing the denominator,
<me>4 x^{3} y + x^{4} \frac{dy}{dx} = 
    (1 + x^{8} y^2) (y^{4} + 4 x y^{3} \frac{dy}{dx}).</me>
Thus
<me>( x^{4} - (4 x y^{3}) (1 + x^{8} y^2) ) \frac{dy}{dx} = 
    y^{4} (1 + x^{8} y^2) - 4 x^{3} y,</me>
and finally
<me>\frac{dy}{dx} = 
\frac{y^{4} (1 + x^{8} y^2) - 4 x^{3} y}{x^{4} - (4 x y^{3}) (1 + x^{8} y^2)}.</me>



</solution>
